  "packageCombos": {
    "deny": [
      {
        "with": "tbl.colortbl",
        "reason": "tbl.colortbl loads \\usepackage[table]{xcolor}, so colortbl patches array again when its line comes after arydshln's, and array loaded first does not stop that; the package fact's colortbl conflict does not see a load made through xcolor's option, and the host does not honour load order. In the copy's batch-3b article.A run all 17 tbl.arydshln branches of the 10 documents where tbl.colortbl came after arydshln stop at 'Illegal pream-token (;)' or \\adl@hline (report.A: 18 of 18); the 22 documents (33 branches) where colortbl came first had no error, and are filed apart too.",
        "status": "untested"
      },
      {
        "with": "general:table",
        "reason": "arydshln's \\multicolumn is not \\long, and every one of General's table ways ends an aligned paragraph in a spanning cell with \\par (\\multicolumn{1}{|>{\\raggedright\\arraybackslash}X|}{{\\bfseries {\\centering Run...\\par}}}); the library's own tables keep \\par out of spanning cells (node.ts noPar). With arydshln's patches in force (no array or colortbl loaded after it) such a document never finishes: the engine's 120 s tool watchdog stops XeTeX and leaves no log. In the copy's article, report, amsart and scrartcl A runs, every document holding tbl.arydshln and such a cell either hung (67, one of them, report.A d478b2bae1389876cf39d, also holding tbl.nicematrix) or compiled with arydshln undone by a colortbl, xcolor[table] or tabularx load after it ('Illegal pream-token (;)', e.g. 47bbc3df1fa8); with arydshln in force and no such cell, 826 compiled and 1 hung (another cause).",
        "status": "untested"
      }
    ]
  }
